1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,493
Introducing TrackMyOPT. Your Chrome extension.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:07,109
Prefill your application. Then review.

3
00:00:07,404 --> 00:00:18,516
Open TrackMyOPT in Chrome. Choose OPT Clock, enter your EAD start date, and save. See unemployment days used and remaining, and manage daily reminders.

4
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:25,365
For STEM, enter your EAD start date. Save to see cumulative unemployment days used and remaining.

5
00:00:25,627 --> 00:00:32,382
OPT Apply Dates uses your program end date and optional DSO recommendation date to show your filing window.

6
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:39,325
For STEM Apply Dates, enter your current OPT expiry and recommendation dates. Calculate your window and countdown.

7
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:41,374
Check case status at a glance.

8
00:00:41,804 --> 00:00:47,322
Prefill supported application fields, review your answers, and check the posting’s sponsorship signal.

9
00:00:47,582 --> 00:00:51,566
Save roles to Wishlist or Applied, then open them in your tracker.

10
00:00:53,271 --> 00:00:57,375
Analyze your résumé against the posting. Review matching keywords and gaps.

11
00:00:57,627 --> 00:01:06,889
Create a tailored résumé. Check the job description, choose a saved, pasted, or uploaded résumé and template, then follow progress. Download the PDF or edit.

12
00:01:07,138 --> 00:01:11,012
Generate a cover letter, review the draft, and save your edits.

13
00:01:11,493 --> 00:01:13,822
Manage saved answers for future applications.

14
00:01:14,071 --> 00:01:19,970
Choose step-by-step or continuous prefill. Guided Autopilot helps navigate steps, without clicking Submit.

15
00:01:20,204 --> 00:01:21,914
Expand or minimize the sidebar.

16
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,961
TrackMyOPT for Chrome.

17
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:27,945
Thanks for watching. Start using TrackMyOPT today.
